MID_EV13_048_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_048_m01_001: Your Majesty, the details for the Heroic Games'\nmain matches have been announced.
MID_EV13_048_m01_002: The matchups were determined while we were\naway from Dagsion.
MID_EV13_048_m01_003: We missed much while we visited Troy's shrine and\nthe forbidden land. Still, we gained much as well.
MID_EV13_048_m01_004: Tell me what you have learned, Bonaventure.
MID_EV13_048_m01_005: Right! Ahem...
MID_EV13_048_m01_006: Many of these names are known to me. It seems they\nwon their bouts as well.
MID_EV13_048_m01_007: But there is one clan I heard no mention of.
MID_EV13_048_m01_008: I noticed that myself and have already looked into it.
MID_EV13_048_m01_009: Sure enough, the inimitable White-Maned Demon's\nclan did not participate in the qualifiers.
MID_EV13_048_m01_010: Interesting. So the final player has taken his\nplace onstage.
MID_EV13_048_m01_021: Our first opponent will be the clan led by Talimun\nof the Vandahl Trading Company.
MID_EV13_048_m01_022: The most troublesome of them all. His motives\nremain opaque to me.
MID_EV13_048_m01_023: It's not just that. The Vandahl Trading Company has\nvast holdings as Dagda's foremost merchant house.
MID_EV13_048_m01_024: An organization of that scale can afford the finest\ntalent on the market.
MID_EV13_048_m01_045: So they're gonna buy their way to victory?\nPretty slimy.
MID_EV13_048_m01_046: Even if we can best Talimun, there will be more\nstrong contenders to come.
MID_EV13_048_m01_041: Yes...our adversaries will all be powerful. But it is\nno matter; let them come.
MID_EV13_048_m01_042: All who stand in our way will be crushed under the\nmight of Saramis. We shall be the victors here.
MID_EV13_048_m01_043: Bare your fangs, all of you. Saramis depends on it.
MID_EV13_104_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_104_m01_001: I'm glad I ran into you, Theodora. I have a favor\nto ask.
MID_EV13_104_m01_002: Your timing is perfect. I have something to discuss\nwith you as well.
MID_EV13_104_m01_003: You do? Well, to start, I've heard that the large ship\nanchored in the harbor is the property of Saramis.
MID_EV13_104_m01_004: The Trafalgar, you mean? Indeed it is.
MID_EV13_104_m01_005: I would like to borrow it. I'll need it for a month.
MID_EV13_104_m01_006: What? Do not be absurd. That is Saramis's flagship.
MID_EV13_104_m01_007: I understand the request is burdensome. But you are\nthe only one who can help here.
MID_EV13_104_m01_008: Even so, it is a large favor. One that has no\nprecedent in our history.
MID_EV13_104_m01_009: Ordinarily, I would brook no such request. But in this\ncase...I owe your people a great debt.
MID_EV13_104_m01_010: Very well. I will consider it, depending on the nature\nof your need. Explain yourself.
MID_EV13_104_m01_011: I must go to the ancient kingdom of Solomon,\neast of the Danann Sea.
MID_EV13_104_m01_012: What I seek may be awaiting me there.
MID_EV13_104_m01_013: I have heard legends of that place. You mean to\ntravel to it yourself?
MID_EV13_104_m01_014: Hmmm...
MID_EV13_104_m01_015: Very well. The Trafalgar is yours to command.
MID_EV13_104_m01_016: Truly? Thank you, Theodora!
MID_EV13_104_m01_017: But not for free. I must ask you to do something\nfor me while you are there.
MID_EV13_104_m01_018: There is a fabled spice in Solomon. I would have\na seedling of the tree which grows it.
MID_EV13_104_m01_019: To search for it on my order would provide at least\na barely plausible excuse for my people.
MID_EV13_104_m01_020: Then, too, that pepper fetches an exorbitant price\nat market.
MID_EV13_104_m01_021: If you can indeed get me one, Saramis will profit\ngreatly by it. A worthy venture, I should say.
MID_EV13_104_m01_022: Consider it done.
MID_EV13_104_m01_023: One other thing, Anatolia. I have been to Kunlun,\nwith Long as my guide.
MID_EV13_104_m01_024: He said as much. He also said that he enjoyed\ntraveling with you.
MID_EV13_104_m01_025: I'd like to visit your kingdom someday as well.
MID_EV13_104_m01_026: To see what our long-lost kin have built—to see how\nthey live.
MID_EV13_104_m01_027: If I win the Heroic Games, I will ask for the gate to\nthe forbidden land to be opened.
MID_EV13_104_m01_028: But that's not enough. I now know that I must also\nchange how the People of the White Egg are viewed.
MID_EV13_104_m01_029: Otherwise, the outside world will never accept them.
MID_EV13_104_m01_030: We share a common ancestry. My people would\nwelcome yours as neighbors.
MID_EV13_104_m01_031: It will not go smoothly, but we will do our utmost to\nease the bumps in the transition.
MID_EV13_104_m01_032: However, you would need to obey Saraminian law.
MID_EV13_104_m01_033: If you would live among us, you must abide by the\ncommandment set to us by Yu Phas.
MID_EV13_104_m01_034: All written language must be abandoned.
MID_EV13_104_m01_035: All of it? I see...
MID_EV13_105_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_105_m01_001: Yu Phas. I have come again to gaze upon your face.
MID_EV13_105_m01_002: Ah, Theodora! I haven't seen you in a while.
MID_EV13_105_m01_003: What?! Was someone watching me?
MID_EV13_105_m01_004: I haven't seen you around. Have you been away\nfrom Dagsion?
MID_EV13_105_m01_005: Oh! What a lovely maiden.
MID_EV13_105_m01_007: Are you...Yu Phas? No...this is not possible.
MID_EV13_105_m01_008: Oh, you didn't know? That mask of mine got broken\nduring a match.
MID_EV13_105_m01_009: "Mask"? Wait. I know that voice. Are you the\ncat priest?!
MID_EV13_105_m01_010: I am...shocked beyond words.
MID_EV13_105_m01_011: Now that I see you unmasked, your face is uncannily\nsimilar to the statue of Yu Phas.
MID_EV13_105_m01_012: What a gift, to share a face with the greatest woman\never to live! I envy you.
MID_EV13_105_m01_013: I wonder about that. All I get from looking at the\nstatue is anxious.
MID_EV13_105_m01_014: Really? Whatever for?
MID_EV13_105_m01_015: The great progenitor god—The Beginning—issued\na decree.
MID_EV13_105_m01_016: Yu Phas and her three sisters were bound never to\nreveal their true faces to anyone.
MID_EV13_105_m01_017: Their duty was to protect the tomb of their father,\nBalor, so his slumber would never be disturbed.
MID_EV13_105_m01_018: You heard this one before, Bona?
MID_EV13_105_m01_019: I... I have not. There is no mention of any such\n"progenitor god" in the oral history.
MID_EV13_105_m01_020: But Yu Phas exposed her true face to Lord Solel.
MID_EV13_105_m01_021: And that was the start of a lot of terrible tragedies.
MID_EV13_105_m01_022: It was the same for me. I wasn't allowed to show my\ntrue face either, but I ended up doing it anyway.
MID_EV13_105_m01_023: I'm worried that there's great punishment in store\nfor me because of it.
MID_EV13_105_m01_024: I'm not certain I follow your logic.
MID_EV13_105_m01_025: It is absurd to live with one's face behind a strange\nmask at the whim of another.
MID_EV13_105_m01_026: I see no reason why you should not be more open.\nUnintentionally or not, the mask is off.
MID_EV13_105_m01_027: This is an opportunity to come to terms with your\nown face. Nothing more.
MID_EV13_105_m01_028: I hope you're right.
MID_EV13_105_m01_029: Beauty like yours tends to draw unwanted attention\nfrom the masses, but you will be fine.
MID_EV13_105_m01_030: Your strength is a match for your beauty, after all.\nShould anyone rouse your ire...
MID_EV13_105_m01_031: simply throw them into Lake Baal. The size of the\nsplash ought to be a sight to see.
MID_EV13_105_m01_032: Heh. I guess.
MID_EV13_105_m01_033: But I'm starting to think I've been in this world\nlonger than I knew.
MID_EV13_105_m01_034: And that long ago, I did something terribly wrong.\nIt scares me.
MID_EV13_105_m01_035: What if Credna made me wear the mask to\nprotect me from my past?
MID_EV13_105_m01_036: Oh! Oh no. I've forgotten an important duty I was\nsupposed to attend to!
MID_EV13_105_m01_037: Plus I just now remembered that this place is off-\nlimits to ordinary people!
MID_EV13_105_m01_038: Oh, I am aware.
MID_EV13_050_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_050_m01_001: What's the matter, boss? You seem kinda out of it.
MID_EV13_050_m01_002: Do I? I thought I hid it better.
MID_EV13_050_m01_003: Yeah, you're not looking so hot.
MID_EV13_050_m01_004: You're not pushing yourself again, are you?
MID_EV13_050_m01_005: We could give up on the whole "long-held dream"\nthing and bow out here.
MID_EV13_050_m01_006: Lilian! How can you show such disrespect to\nHer Majesty?!
MID_EV13_050_m01_007: <NCA>Hear Lilian out.
MID_EV13_050_m01_008: <NCB>Pay her no heed.
MID_EV13_050_m01_009: <ACA>I mean, we just went to all the trouble to get another\nwarding chain.
MID_EV13_050_m01_010: <ACA>Aren't you worried that using the arm too much will\npush it past its limits and break it again?
MID_EV13_050_m01_011: <ACA>Is winning so important that you'd risk your life\nlike that?
MID_EV13_050_m01_012: <ACA>I feel like there's gotta be some other way.
MID_EV13_050_m01_013: <ACA>Hmm. She may have a point.
MID_EV13_050_m01_014: <ACA>Withdrawing from the tournament here to live in\npeace at Megaira may preserve the warding chain.
MID_EV13_050_m01_015: <ACA>It could give Your Majesty many more years of\nsanity in the long run.
MID_EV13_050_m01_016: Bonaventure, you once said that a kingdom is its\npeople. I believe you were right.
MID_EV13_050_m01_017: Ah, yes, when Prince Dyan called his council\nof chieftains.
MID_EV13_050_m01_018: Oh, really?
MID_EV13_050_m01_019: Allow me to expand on that idea. Hear me, all of you.
MID_EV13_050_m01_020: I sometimes think of a kingdom as a ship. Its people\nare not passengers, but sailors.
MID_EV13_050_m01_021: Each plays a role in the proper operation of the ship.\nIt runs according to their efforts.
MID_EV13_050_m01_022: Who, then, is the queen? Most would call her the\nship's captain, who orders her crew. I disagree.
MID_EV13_050_m01_023: A queen must be more like a navigator.
MID_EV13_050_m01_024: She reads the desires of the people and charts a\ncourse to take their kingdom where it must go.
MID_EV13_050_m01_025: That is the proper role of a queen, as I see it.
MID_EV13_050_m01_026: Determining this course is not simple. To misread the\nfluctuating currents ends in disaster.
MID_EV13_050_m01_027: And no one can say how long a ship may\nremain seaworthy.
MID_EV13_050_m01_028: That is why it is also the queen's role to avoid the\nhazards of temptation in the populace.
MID_EV13_050_m01_029: A kingdom where the people's dreams are twisted\ntoward evil cannot stand for long.
MID_EV13_050_m01_030: The star we must navigate by is the spirit inherited\nfrom our ancestors.
MID_EV13_050_m01_031: Faith is like a guide along the course to that end.\nThe people of Saramis live by it.
MID_EV13_050_m01_032: Someone must be the one to chart such a course.
MID_EV13_050_m01_033: But none of that explains why you've gotta kill\nyourself doing it.
MID_EV13_050_m01_034: Right now we have a golden opportunity.
MID_EV13_050_m01_035: If I can fulfill the long-held dream of Saramis at the\ncost of my life, I would be churlish not to.
MID_EV13_050_m01_036: Your selflessness is admirable, but you are still\nyoung, Your Majesty.
MID_EV13_050_m01_037: I would never blame you for putting your own\nwell-being first.
MID_EV13_050_m01_038: When the people of Saramis are fulfilled and\nhappy, then I shall be happy as well.
MID_EV13_050_m01_039: As befits a queen. But you are not only a queen—\nyou are a human being.
MID_EV13_050_m01_040: Do not hurry to your death while you still have a\nright to happiness in life.
MID_EV13_050_m01_041: On the day of my coronation, when I swore my oath\nto the people of Saramis, I renounced that right.
MID_EV13_050_m01_042: This right arm may consume me whole, and soon.
MID_EV13_050_m01_043: But I will accept that fate gladly if the people know\nwhat I did for them as their queen.
MID_EV13_050_m01_044: And a queen can't compromise a little?
MID_EV13_050_m01_045: I don't think I'll ever quite get it.
MID_EV13_050_m01_046: A queen's power comes with a duty to others, Lilian.
MID_EV13_050_m01_047: Her Majesty understands the gravity of her actions\nbetter than anyone. It shapes her life.
MID_EV13_050_m01_048: Sure, yeah, it's just...not how I think.
MID_EV13_050_m01_049: You can at least let us help with whatever we can.\nNo need to shoulder it all yourself.
MID_EV13_050_m01_050: Lean on us a little more, alright?
MID_EV13_050_m01_051: I shall do so. Thank you.
MID_EV13_049_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_049_m01_001: Well, well, well. We make quite the pair, don't we?\nThe queen of Saramis meets the king of merchants!
MID_EV13_049_m01_002: Care to make this interesting? If our crews are\ngoing to fight, why not raise the stakes a little?
MID_EV13_049_m01_003: Let's say... If I win, I get free use of Saramis's ports.\nAnd free means free. Tax exempt and everything.
MID_EV13_049_m01_004: Then you must ante something of equal value.\nWhat would you wager against this prize?
MID_EV13_049_m01_005: Hmm... How does three million gold sound?
MID_EV13_049_m01_006: Like an insult. Free use of our ports would let you\nbuy spices and gems available cheaply in the south.
MID_EV13_049_m01_007: The profit resulting from such an unfettered venture\nwould be immense.
MID_EV13_049_m01_008: Next to what you would stand to gain, three million\ngold is a paltry sum.
MID_EV13_049_m01_009: Moreover, with access to the ocean ports of Alecto,\nyou would not be limited to the Danann Sea.
MID_EV13_049_m01_010: Your business could thereby expand by orders of\nmagnitude. Three million? Laughable.
MID_EV13_049_m01_011: So, no deal, then? Have it your way... It seemed like\na reasonable enough offer to me.
MID_EV13_049_m01_012: {SetColor=Gray}Here I thought this queen had muscle for brains,\nbut I guess she knows a thing or two.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_049_m01_013: Ah well, I'll let it go for now. Though I do appreciate\nyou taking my offer so seriously, Majesty.
MID_EV13_049_m01_014: Do not be so hasty. I have a counteroffer.
MID_EV13_049_m01_015: Should Saramis ever face an existential threat...
MID_EV13_049_m01_016: Vandahl Trading will support us with all the funds,\nsupplies, and personnel it can bring to bear.
MID_EV13_049_m01_017: Not for free, mind you. Should it come to that,\nI would consider it a debt incurred.
MID_EV13_049_m01_018: A debt I would vow to repay, no matter how long\nit takes. Provided the interest rate is low.
MID_EV13_049_m01_019: If Saramis faces an existential threat, huh?
MID_EV13_049_m01_020: Yes. Not to me—to my kingdom.
MID_EV13_049_m01_021: What, have the Mosa down south got you spooked?
MID_EV13_049_m01_022: The Mosa are no threat to us. Surely you know the\nhistory of Saramis—of Damascar.
MID_EV13_049_m01_023: I am preparing to ward off a greater enemy than\nthey could ever be.
MID_EV13_049_m01_024: I must consider the possibility that our allies of today\nmay turn their knives on us tomorrow.
MID_EV13_049_m01_025: Cautious bordering on paranoid...yet practical.\nI accept your terms.
MID_EV13_049_m01_026: I hope he's true to his word on this.
MID_EV13_049_m01_027: Of course I am! Integrity is a merchant's greatest\nasset—next to an eye for opportunity, you see.
MID_EV13_049_m01_028: My, but his ears are sharp.
MID_EV13_049_m01_029: {SetColor=Gray}"Existential threat," huh?{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_049_m01_030: {SetColor=Gray}That could end up costing me quite a bit more than\nthree million gold.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_049_m01_031: {SetColor=Gray}It's certainly not ideal... I'll just have to make sure\nwe don't lose this match.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_051_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_051_m01_001: I know when I'm bested, Majesty. Well done.
MID_EV13_051_m01_002: You seem oddly cheerful for a man who has lost a\nhefty wager. Can I rely on you to honor the deal?
MID_EV13_051_m01_003: Sure. I thought it over, you see, and I decided there's\nno downside to supporting a queen like you.
MID_EV13_051_m01_004: Should the time come, I shall dispatch a messenger\nto you immediately.
MID_EV13_051_m01_005: While I, for my part, will be hoping such a time\nnever comes.
MID_EV13_051_m01_006: Until then, I'll be praying—with whatever godliness\nI possess—that you get your wish.
MID_EV13_051_m01_007: That is greatly appreciated. What are your plans\nfrom here?
MID_EV13_051_m01_008: My plans? Oh, back to the usual for me, following\nwind and whimsy wherever they lead.
MID_EV13_051_m01_009: Talimun! That won't do!
MID_EV13_051_m01_010: We have a mountain of unresolved problems on the\ndocket. The Morfis thing is just the start.
MID_EV13_051_m01_011: They certainly have a lot of irons in the fire.
MID_EV13_051_m01_012: Not for nothing are they Dagda's foremost merchant\nhouse. The man clearly has sterling aides.
MID_EV13_051_m01_013: Queen Theodora! I have a report.
MID_EV13_051_m01_014: Now? Her Majesty is tired, Lysander. You are\ndisrupting her rest.
MID_EV13_051_m01_015: But it's urgent news from Megaira. Prince Dyan\nhas vanished from his prison!
MID_EV13_051_m01_016: I don't have many details, but an early investigation\nsuggests he had outside help.
MID_EV13_051_m01_017: Of all the times, why now?!
MID_EV13_051_m01_018: No. He chose this moment deliberately.
MID_EV13_051_m01_019: Seriously?! Prince Dyan just vanished?
MID_EV13_051_m01_020: Your Majesty, his co-conspirators may have waited\nfor us to be away to advance their plots.
MID_EV13_051_m01_021: Haah...
MID_EV13_051_m01_022: We have come too far for distractions. We shall\ncontinue with the Heroic Games.
MID_EV13_051_m01_023: Tell the chancellor to continue the search for Dyan\nand to be wary of any related activity.
MID_EV13_051_m01_024: And tell him to report anything suspicious to me\nimmediately, no matter how insignificant.
MID_EV13_051_m01_025: Your Majesty...
MID_EV13_051_m01_026: It was a mistake to show him mercy because he is\nmy only remaining kin. I was naïve.
MID_EV13_051_m01_027: I should have killed him where he stood to cut out\nthe rot.
MID_EV13_051_m01_028: That said, this incident provides us with all the\njustification we need.
MID_EV13_051_m01_029: I am certain that once we catch Prince Dyan this\ntime, no one will object to his execution.
MID_EV13_051_m01_030: Yes...that is true enough.